# Cursor Quality Checks & Rules

## Mandatory 90% Per-File Unit Test Code Coverage Benchmark

- Every source file in this Java Maven workspace must achieve at least **90% coverage** across ALL metrics:
  - Instructions / Statements (>= 90%)
  - Lines (>= 90%)
  - Branches (>= 90%)
  - Methods / Functions (>= 90%)
  - Cyclomatic Complexity (>= 90%)
  - Class (>= 90%)
- Zero file exemptions. No `<excludes>` allowed.
- All unit tests must conform to global timeouts (10s default per test).
- Before declaring task completion on ANY change, run:
  ```powershell
  mvn clean test jacoco:report
  ```
- If any file falls below 90% on any parameter, the build will fail immediately (`haltOnFailure=true`). Fix all test coverage deficiencies before completing.
